version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A Python derivatives pricing toolkit with Black-Scholes analytics, binomial
  and trinomial trees, and Monte Carlo methods including antithetic and
  control variates, designed around explicit numerical error control. The
  Monte Carlo pricers run on three interchangeable back ends: pure Python,
  NumPy and C++20.
